  "irVersion": 8,
  "notes": {
    "fit-check": "Decides, one level at a time, whether a value of one type fits where another is expected.",
    "fit-check.calcs.fits": "The kind of a value (given) and the expected kind; for an enumeration value, the kind of its members (base) and whether they are all members of the expected enumeration (subset); for atoms, whether they are of the same sort. Anything fits where any is expected and any fits anywhere. Where JSON is expected, anything fits but nothing (void) and a temporal formula. Null fits only where an optional value is expected. Where an optional value is expected, an optional value is compared inside (inner), and any other value is compared with what is inside the expected type (unwrap). An optional value fits nowhere else. Where an enumeration is expected, only an enumeration whose members are a subset fits. An enumeration fits where its base kind is expected. Atoms fit only atoms of the same sort. Where a record, list, set or map is expected, the same kind is compared inside, and anything else does not fit. Otherwise only the same kind fits."
  },
